<article class="env-remark" id="03FH">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03FH">Remark <span data-tag="03FH">35.8.6</span>.</a> Remark <a href="/tag/070R" data-tag="070R">35.8.4</a> and Lemma <a href="/tag/070S" data-tag="070S">35.8.5</a> have the following applications: </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
Let $S$ be a scheme. The construction $\mathcal{F} \mapsto \mathcal{F}^ a$ is the pullback under the morphism of ringed sites $\text{id}_{\tau , Zar} : ((\mathit{Sch}/S)_\tau , \mathcal{O}) \to (S_{Zar}, \mathcal{O})$ or the morphism $\text{id}_{small, {\acute{e}tale}, Zar} : (S_{\acute{e}tale}, \mathcal{O}) \to (S_{Zar}, \mathcal{O})$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
Let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism of schemes. For any of the morphisms $f_{sites}$ of ringed sites of Remark <a href="/tag/070R" data-tag="070R">35.8.4</a> we have 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  (f^*\mathcal{F})^ a = f_{sites}^*\mathcal{F}^ a.  \]
</div>
<p>
 This follows from (1) and the fact that pullbacks are compatible with compositions of morphisms of ringed sites, see Modules on Sites, Lemma <a href="/tag/03D8" data-tag="03D8">18.13.3</a>. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>